Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P6.1 language select (CNTY_SEL) fills 16:9

The language select of the EU disc (CNTY_SEL, the "SELECT LANGUAGE" screen
shown at every start; the US disc carries the overlay too) ran with gutter 0, a
4:3 picture pillarboxed. port/options/widescreen.c gives the overlay the menu
gutter (US 0x157, EU 0x165) and:

- the scrolling background (96 px period) is drawn twice more, 96 pixels to
  each side, as patch 0053;
- the language list panel starts where it did and runs to the 16:9 right edge
  (DW3_MENU_EXTEND), with its open pivot; the flags, the names and the
  highlight bars stay;
- the title strip is widened at its middle (DW3_MENU_BAND, split -160): its
  "SELECT LANGUAGE" label hangs from the left edge and its tiles run to the
  right edge;
- the logo band hangs from the left edge (DW3_MENU_LEFT) with its pivot.

DW3_MENU_BAND's frame limit goes from 64 to 160 parts (the list panel has 60
parts and the helper needs room for the copies it adds). Drawing only; off
(gutter 0) every position is the PS1 one.

--- a/src/menus/country_select/country_select.c
+++ b/src/menus/country_select/country_select.c
@@ -1,4 +1,7 @@
 #include "menus/country_select.h"
+#if PORT_HOST
+#include "port_widescreen.h"
+#endif
 
 RECT CNTY_SEL_screenRect = {0, 0, SCREEN_WIDTH, SCREEN_HEIGHT};
 RECT CNTY_SEL_vramRect = {0, 0, 1024, 512};
@@ -90,6 +93,14 @@
     /* The background repeats every 96 pixels */
     offset = (s16)((s16)(task->scroll / 2) % 96);
     sprite.draw(FILE_CACHE.getEntry(CNTY_SEL_SPRITES), SPRITE_BACKGROUND, offset, offset);
+#if PORT_HOST
+    /* Widescreen: the pattern repeats every 96 pixels; two more copies cover the side gutters
+       at every scroll (patch 0053's recipe) */
+    if (dw3_port_widescreen_px() > 0) {
+        sprite.draw(FILE_CACHE.getEntry(CNTY_SEL_SPRITES), SPRITE_BACKGROUND, offset - 96, offset);
+        sprite.draw(FILE_CACHE.getEntry(CNTY_SEL_SPRITES), SPRITE_BACKGROUND, offset + 96, offset);
+    }
+#endif
 }
 
